<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kuksha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. early 12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kuksha was a monk of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv-pechersk-lavra">Kiev Monastery of the Caves</a> who preached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> to the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vyatichians">Vyatichi</a> in the late 11th or early 12th century and was killed by them together with his disciple Nikon. Venerated as a martyr, he is a saint of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox Church</a>, and his relics are kept in the Near Caves of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> monastery.</p></div>
